<Base title="Parameter semantics · RoboWiki" description="How torque, speed, source tiers and missing values are defined.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl py-6">
    <h1>Parameter semantics</h1>
    <p>One hard rule on this site: <strong>torque and speed always mean the output side (gearbox included).</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>A</code> tier = every field checked against a vendor manual. <code>B</code> = public web page, not cross-checked. <code>C</code> = relayed.</li>
      <li><code>—</code> means <em>not published</em>, not <em>not supported</em>, and never <code>0</code>. Do not fill gaps from similar parts.</li>
      <li>Missing is missing: a blank field is a claim we could not source, not a value of zero.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Example: the DJI M3508 manual quotes 0.16 N·m at the motor side. We publish 3.07 N·m at the output side (× 19.203208556, protocol value 3591/187) and keep the original number and the arithmetic in that part's notes.</p>
    <p>Ordering always goes by spec and measured data — never by who contributed more.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
